**v0.118.0+.** A dynamic group whose rules match on a field the device reports about itself is not used to decide where something **runs**. Because the device sets these values itself, Breeze skips the group as an execution target. These fields are:

- hostname and display name;
- tags and device role;
- last user;
- agent version and Helper version;
- installed software (installed or not installed);
- any custom field.

Such a group is skipped as a target of scripts, automations, software policies and update rings. It is also skipped by the automation, software, remote-access, PAM, maintenance, OneDrive and Assist policy features. Patch and backup assignments still resolve through it, and so does every non-execution use: listing members, filters, views and reports.

Each skip is recorded in the audit log with the fields that caused it. Where you target a group interactively, for example from an update ring or a deployment, the response also shows a warning naming the group.

To target these devices, build the group on fields Breeze accepts for targeting, such as organization, site, OS, hardware, network facts or metrics. Or use a static group.

```json
{
  "operator": "AND",
  "conditions": [
    { "field": "osType", "operator": "equals", "value": "windows" },
    {
      "operator": "OR",
      "conditions": [
        { "field": "status", "operator": "equals", "value": "offline" },
        { "field": "daysSinceLastSeen", "operator": "greaterThan", "value": 7 }
      ]
    }
  ]
}
```

