A client on the stateless `2026-07-28` protocol that declares URL-mode elicitation (`clientCapabilities.elicitation.url`) gets a richer first answer than `pending_approval`. The result is `resultType: "input_required"` with one `elicitation/create` request in **URL mode** that points at the Breeze approval page, plus a signed `requestState`:

```json
{
  "resultType": "input_required",
  "inputRequests": {
    "breeze_approval": {
      "method": "elicitation/create",
      "params": { "mode": "url", "message": "…", "url": "https://app.example.com/approvals#intent-5b0c1c7e-…" }
    }
  },
  "requestState": "<signed>"
}
```

Breeze never sends form-mode elicitation, and a client that declares only `elicitation: {}` (form) or is on an earlier protocol gets the plain `pending_approval` result. The URL carries only the request id; opening it needs a Breeze login.

The client retries the same `tools/call` (same tool and arguments) with `requestState` and `inputResponses.breeze_approval.action`:

- `accept` waits up to `MCP_APPROVAL_WAIT_MS` for the decision. A finished request returns its outcome (the real result when `completed`, an error result when rejected, failed, expired or cancelled). A request still waiting returns `pending_approval`; poll `get_action_status` from there.
- `decline` cancels the request (needs `ai:write`).
- `cancel` (dismissed) leaves the request pending and returns its status.

The `requestState` is bound to the credential, tool, arguments and a 10-minute lifetime; any mismatch returns `-32602` with `data.reason` (`invalid_request_state` or `request_state_expired`, the latter with `data.actionId` for the same credential). A retry never files a new request.

